# SSTIM by example, 4 of 4: record that you actually delivered it.
#
# sstim-profile: full
#
# Three objects, kept apart on purpose, and the separation is the lesson.
#
#   Preset               how one engine was configured. Engine-dependent.
#   SessionSpecification what was planned for this run.
#   SessionInstance      what happened, including how it ended.
#
# The preset points back at the stimulus specification from examples 01 and 02
# through sstim:specifiedBy. That link is asserted by whoever measured or
# derived it, never inferred: what a configuration actually produces depends on
# the engine, the transducer and the room. Asserting it is what lets two labs
# on different hardware claim they delivered the same stimulus, and lets a
# reader disagree with the claim.
#
# Note what this file does not carry: no participant identifier, no free text,
# and nothing that could identify a person. Self-report and observation terms
# exist in the session module; whether an identifiable observation belongs in a
# published graph is a question this example does not answer for you.

@prefix ex:      <https://example.org/stimuli/> .
@prefix dct:     <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sstim:   <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix sstim-v: <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:alpha-preset-webaudio a sstim:Preset ;
    rdfs:label "Example Lab 10 Hz audiovisual preset, Web Audio build 3"@en ;
    dct:description "One engine's configuration for the stimulus specification in examples 01 and 02. Another engine realising the same specification would be a different preset and an equally valid one."@en ;
    sstim:specifiedBy ex:alpha-audiovisual ;
    sstim:durationSeconds 600 .

ex:run-2026-09-17-001-spec a sstim:SessionSpecification, prov:Plan ;
    rdfs:label "Planned run 001, 17 September 2026"@en ;
    dct:created "2026-09-17T09:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    sstim:referencesPreset ex:alpha-preset-webaudio ;
    sstim:durationSeconds 600 ;
    sstim:masterVolume 0.20 .

# completionStatus is one of completed, interrupted or abandoned, and the
# honest value matters more than the tidy one. A run that ended early is data;
# a run recorded as complete because the field looked better that way is not.
ex:run-2026-09-17-001 a sstim:SessionInstance ;
    rdfs:label "Run 001, 17 September 2026"@en ;
    sstim:usesSpecification ex:run-2026-09-17-001-spec ;
    sstim:actualDurationSeconds 600 ;
    sstim:completionStatus "completed" ;
    sstim:hasDeliveryModality sstim-v:modalityAuditory, sstim-v:modalityVisual ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-09-17T09:01:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-09-17T09:11:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
